foreign  welcome to another installment of Harry  Potter Theory today we're going to be  discussing the 10 largest magical  creatures the behemoths of The Wizarding  World this list was particularly  difficult to make as the exact  specifications of each creature height  weight Etc are not easy to come by  suffice to say the honorable mentions  list following the main list is pretty  long as well I don't think you'll be  able to guess all 10 but leave a comment  down below before you start and see if  you're right at the end anyway I won't  dawdle here are the 10 most enormous  magical creatures 10. Giants ironically  the aptly named giant is the smallest  creature on this list but that's a rare  position for them to be in Giants are  incredibly powerful creatures that tend  to live out their lives in tribes  completely separate from the rest of the  Wizarding Community they are smarter  than trolls stupider than humans and  their innate bloodthirsty Nature has  typically resulted in their own  population control the secret to Giant's  power is in their name they are giant in  fact they are larger than almost any  other magical creature equal in physical  strength to dragons and highly resistant  to spells Giants can grow to be  approximately 20 to 25 feet in height  which puts the largest Giants at about  twice the size of Hagrid who is 12 feet  tall what's important to note however is  that Robbie Coltrane in the films was  portrayed to be eight foot six therefore  the actual size of giants is about three  times what we see from Hagrid on screen  nine three-headed dog they were looking  straight into the eyes of a monstrous  dog a dog that filled the whole space  between ceiling and floor it had three  heads three pairs of rolling mad eyes  three noses twitching and quivering in  their Direction  three drooling mouths saliva hanging in  Slippery robes from yellowish fangs the  creature described above is of course  fluffy Hagrid's three-headed dog that  once guarded the Philosopher's Stone  three-headed dogs were very rare  creatures that held from Greece the  introduction of fluffy in Harry Potter  is undoubtedly an homage to Cerberus or  The Hound of Hades from Greek mythology  given that fluffy filled the whole space  between ceiling and floor and that  Hogwarts boasted some impressively high  ceilings I'd be willing to bet that  fluffy was at least 25 to 30 feet tall  eight horned serpent horned serpents are  large horned magical snakes with a few  different variations in species that  inhabit bodies of water and possess all  sorts of unusual abilities their horns  are used in one cause and was notably  used in the wand of ilvermorny founder  is old Sayer the core of these ones by  vibrates when parcel tongue is being  spoken and warns the owner of danger by  emitting a low musical tone horned  serpents also exist outside of Harry  Potter in folklore and the general  consensus is that these creatures are at  least 30 feet in length and weigh over  one thousand pounds 7. irumpent irumpens  are large gray African beasts that may  be mistaken for a rhinoceros at a  distance they have thick hides that  repel most charms and curses a large  sharp horn upon its nose and a long  rope-like tail and a rampant does appear  in Fantastic Beasts and let me just say  that this thing is colossal in fact it's  been expressed that female arampans can  grow up to five times the size of a  non-magical hippopotamus which has a  similar body type this would put the  largest a rampants at nearly 7.5 meters  in height and almost 15 meters in length  the rampant is listed as a medium-sized  creature in some places but that is  simply untrue 6. basilisk basilisks are  enormous Serpentine creatures that were  originally created by a dark wizard by  the name of Harpo The fowl of the many  fearsome beasts and monsters that roam  our land there is none more Curious or  more deadly than the Basilisk known also  as the king of serpents this snake which  may reach gigantic size and live many  hundreds of years is born from a  chicken's egg hatched beneath a toad its  methods of killing our most wondrous for  aside from its steadily and venomous  fangs the Basilisk has a murderous stare  and all who are fixed with the beam of  its eye shall suffer instant death  spiders flee before the Basilisk for it  is their mortal enemy and the Basilisk  flees only from the crowing of the  rooster which is fatal to it in size  basilisks are enormous creatures growing  up to 50 feet in length on some accounts  60 feet not only that but they're the  Ultimate Weapon possessing giant fangs  protective scales and a gaze that can  kill you instantly the Basilisk used in  the film was about 80 feet in length  according to prop Creator Robert Blairs  so if you want to imagine the real size  subtract about 37.5 percent 5. dragons  there's no wave watched or read Harry  Potter without seeing or reading about a  dragon or two dragons are giant winged  fire breathing beasts that incite fear  in the hearts of even bravest witches  and wizards they play an integral role  in this series and are even mentioned in  the Hogwarts motto dracon dormin nanquam  Didi Landes which literally translates  to never tickle a sleeping dragon  dragons also bear the potential to be  extremely destructive classified as a  category 5x Beast by the ministry of  magic  but whether they fall in terms of the  largest creatures to uncover that we'll  have to figure out what type of dragon  in Harry Potter there are all sorts of  dragons referenced hailing from all  different locations but as it turns out  the three biggest are the Norwegian  Ridgeback hebridian black and of course  the Behemoth that is the Ukrainian iron  belly the Norwegian Ridgeback and  hebridium black are roughly 30 feet in  length and the Ukrainian iron belly is  doubled at at 60 feet I'd also like to  give an honorable mention here to  women's as they fall somewhat into the  same category as dragons 4. giant squid  giant squids also exist in the Muggle  world but the one in Harry Potter is  purported to be magical in some capacity  and that's why it's on this list the  giant squid in Harry Potter lived in the  great lake near the grounds of Hogwarts  Castle and despite the squid being  portrayed as a fair inspiring symbol the  giant squid near Hogwarts was actually  rather tame a self-domesticated creature  that did nothing but occasionally play  with students while muggle giant squids  are somewhere in the realm of 12 to 13  meters long for females the one in Harry  Potter is supposed to be upwards of 70  feet not bad 3. sea serpent sea serpents  were aquatic magical beasts of immense  size found in oceans all across the  world in appearance they have a  snake-like body paired with a horse-like  head as well as rows of sharp teeth but  despite their immense size and capacity  to do damage sea serpents much like the  giant squid have a fairly peaceful  temperament but just how big rc7s  apparently over 100 feet this makes them  the largest creatures on this list so  far by a huge margin they are absolutely  colossal but if you happen to find  yourself near one fear not as there have  been no reported attacks on man or  wizard kind 2. nundu next up we have the  nundu noon Do's are magical beasts  somewhat resembling a line that have a  reputation for being the most  destructive and Powerful creatures in  the entire Wizarding World at least when  they're Untamed but how big are they  well this one's a bit of a mess because  the nundu has been very differently  portrayed from book to film you see the  nundu actually appears in both the book  and film versions of Fantastic Beasts  but they are not even remotely  consistent with one another in their  portrayal in the films the nundu is  certainly large but nothing even  remotely comparable to the upper  echelons of this list the book however  shows the nundu as an absolutely  colossal creature that dwarves  everything on the list with the  exception of the number one spot there's  also some Canon that perhaps backs up  just how massive the nundu is apparently  it takes up to 100 witches and wizards  working together to subdue a nundu where  it only takes a dozen to stun a dragon  this could be relevant to the creature's  size but this fact in conjunction with  how it is portrayed in the book and  tells me that it probably really is  quite massive it's also quite possible  that the small nundu in newt's  Commander's briefcase was simply  underdeveloped because it was young 1.  Okami I know what you're thinking Okami  is the largest creatures let me explain  first of all what is an Okami the Okami  is found in the Far East and India a  plumed two-legged winged creature with a  serpentine body it feeds mainly on rats  and birds though has been known to carry  off monkeys the occamy is aggressive to  all who approach it particularly in  defense of its eggs and while the Okami  may not look particularly impressive it  does possess one exceptionally powerful  ability it grows to fit available space  this ability is referred to as granap  Texas so while the Okami may not look  particularly large in some environments  its capacity to grow means that it could  technically outgrow any other creature  provided the space is big enough  and that concludes a list creatures that  narrowly miss the list include Acro  mantulas at 15 feet yetis at 15 feet  trolls at 12 feet manticores at 10 to 15  feet chimeras grap horns sphinxers  Thunderbirds raims and blast ended  screws to name a handful if you enjoy  the content please like the video and  subscribe to the channel until next time  remember imperfect understanding is  often more dangerous than ignorance  [Music]

